title: 'Gnomon spec v3.4: voice approvals (P8-D58..D62) written; OPEN 14 awaits founder'
summary: |-
  docs/specs/gnomon.md is now v3.4, up from 1148 to 1284 lines. The main addition is the new §14.7 Voice approvals:
  - separate reversible and gate arms, each opened by fresh presence;
  - reversible cards are targeted by deck ordinal or label; gate cards need a secret handle plus a 2-word challenge;
  - hold, echo and undo;
  - the TTS phrase mask, interception and the 750 ms mute;
  - grant-row toggles with a judgment sub-class for D61;
  - the never-by-voice list.

  The changes ripple through §0, §3.1, §3.4, §4–5, §9, §11, §12.6, §14, §15, §19 (M4.5 and M4.6), §20, §22, §A.4 and a §16 Windows row. Appendix A was regenerated with compile71.py (zero unoracled). The builder took the stricter Aegis option where the reviews were silent: separate arms, no implicit single-card target, arming only from the wrapper or a native client, a playback gate on both classes. It also fixed a contradiction in Aegis's design: handles are shown or spoken by the arming connection, never by the voice child.

  OPEN 14 for the founder:
  - (a) Decision-count ceilings: the defaults of 30 and 3 are the maxima until ruled.
  - (b) Conversation mode for gate class.
  - (c) S26-L3, deny-by-voice on every card kind.
  - (d) Whether companion presence (Watch) replaces the gate arm.
